    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full `./mvnw test` run is **BUILD SUCCESS** with `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change was implemented in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, the `POST /api/owners` create handler:\n\n- Added a dedicated logger named `AUDIT` (`LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`).\n- After a successful `saveOwner(owner)` \u2014 the point where the owner has its id, generated `customerCode`, and stamped `registrationDate` populated \u2014 it emits an audit line containing all three:\n  ```\n  AUDIT.info(\"owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n      owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n  ```\n\nThe line is emitted only on the success path (after all the capacity/conflict guards that return early), so rejected creates produce no audit record. The `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` test, which captures the `AUDIT` logger and asserts a line contains the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`, now passes.",
