        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe audit emission sits in the one unit that already owns owner-creation orchestration. In this codebase `addOwner` holds all the create-time business rules inline (capacity, household, telephone, and city checks), so the controller \u2014 not the service \u2014 is where \"owner creation\" logic already lives; placing the audit line immediately after `saveOwner` is consistent with that and reads naturally.\n\n- The `AUDIT` logger is a standard `private static final` SLF4J field, named exactly per the spec, and is the only logger of its kind here, so there's no duplication or competing audit mechanism to reuse (V2's owner controller only lists owners; V1 is the sole create path).\n- The addition is minimal and additive \u2014 a single log call at the correct point in the flow (after a successful save, before building the response) \u2014 and doesn't turn the method or class into a catch-all.\n\nNo structural changes needed."
